![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Similarly, the numeric comparisons for `acceptedCountThresholdMet` and `candidateOnlyRatio` are performed directly against `acceptedCountRequired` and `maxCandidateOnlyRatio` without verifying if they are valid finite numbers. If these values are `null` due to missing or malformed configuration, the comparisons can erroneously evaluate to `true`. Explicitly verify that both threshold values are valid finite numbers before performing the comparisons.

```javascript
  const acceptedCountRequired =
    promotionRun.threshold_context.threshold_values.accepted_count_required_for_rag_manifest;
  const maxCandidateOnlyRatio =
    promotionRun.threshold_context.threshold_values.max_candidate_only_ratio_for_rag_manifest;
  const acceptedCountThresholdMet =
    Number.isFinite(acceptedCountRequired) &&
    acceptedItems.length >= acceptedCountRequired;
  const acceptedDeferralActive = promotionRun.validator_backed_deferral?.active === true;
  const reviewDeferralActive = promotionRun.validator_backed_review_deferral?.active === true;
  const manifestStatus = acceptedDeferralActive && reviewDeferralActive
    ? 'rag_ready_with_accepted_growth_and_review_deferral'
    : acceptedDeferralActive
      ? 'rag_ready_with_accepted_growth_deferral'
      : reviewDeferralActive
        ? 'rag_ready_with_review_deferral'
        : acceptedCountThresholdMet &&
          Number.isFinite(maxCandidateOnlyRatio) &&
          candidateOnlyRatio <= maxCandidateOnlyRatio
          ? 'rag_ready'
          : 'not_ready_threshold_failed';
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Ensure that threshold values are explicitly verified as valid finite numbers before performing numeric comparisons (such as `>=` or `<=`) in JavaScript. This prevents comparisons against `null` (which can occur when configuration files are missing or malformed) from erroneously evaluating to `true` due to null coercion to `0`.
</details>

